  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 99-1823, Equal Employment Opportunity Commission v. Waffle House, Inc. Mr. Clement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent Waffle House and Eric Baker agreed to arbitrate rather than litigate disputes between them. That agreement precludes Waffle House and Baker from having an action take place between them in court. But the EEOC was not a party to that agreement. Accordingly, the agreement does not preclude the EEOC's ability to bring a public enforcement action against Waffle House, nor does it limit the remedies available to the EEOC in such an action. Title VII gives the EEOC a public enforcement action that's independent of and, in many respects, superior to the individual employee's cause of action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Paul D. Clement",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: My understanding is that the EEOC picked this case because this case -- the events here took place in 1994. So, the ADA was still quite new at the time that this -- that this case took place, and I think the EEOC was concerned that employers were not sure of what their obligations under the ADA were. So, they picked this case to litigate to help establish what employers' obligations were under the EEOC --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Then I think your answer has got to be that the settlement clearly does not bind the Government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Then your objection is the transmogrification, not to the -- not to the recognition of the agreement as such."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Actually the EEOC is of the opinion that the -- that the individual could bring an arbitration action at that point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is a consequence, though, of the view that they cannot intervene in the EEOC's enforcement action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gordon",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the EEOC is acting on behalf of Mr. Baker."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Questioner",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But isn't there a public interest?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gordon",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GORDON: Well, there is, of course, the -- the strong Federal policy favoring arbitration, the text of the Federal Arbitration Act that says, we're going to enforce agreements."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here respondent seeks not only to bind the EEOC to the results of an arbitration, but to prevent the EEOC from seeking all remedies even when there hasn't been any arbitration proceeding initiated at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-99-1823",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "414632c01a7decef6f679163735a9b1420f98c250211cbb592f5c64c44af886c",
      "evidence_id": "ev-414632c01a7d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Mr. Clement. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:01 a.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
